    "answer": "presbyopia/age-related-longsightedness/farsightedness",
    "mnemonic": "An <kanji>elderly</kanji> <kanji>eyeball</kanji> is one that can't see things close up. That's why this word means <vocabulary>farsightedness</vocabulary>. But this is the kind of farsightedness that only comes with age. So you have to be an elderly oldey to have <ja>老眼</ja>.",
